The Flyweight Design Pattern is a structural pattern that minimizes memory usage
by sharing common object data instead of duplicating it.

When to use this pattern-
1. When memory is limited.
2. When objects share data.
   -Intrinsic Data : Shared among objects and remain same once defined the values.
   -Extrinsic Data : Changes based on client input. differ from one object to another.
3. Creation of object is expensive.

🧠 Core Idea
Split object state into:
🔹 Intrinsic State (shared)
Common data
Stored inside flyweight
Reused across objects
🔹 Extrinsic State (unique)
Context-specific
Passed from outside